// Crossing-voice horizontal note-collision: the lower voice (voice 2, stem-down)
// crosses ABOVE the upper voice (voice 1, stem-up), so voice 1's stems would
// pierce voice 2's noteheads. LilyPond's note-collision "meshing" fallback nudges
// the crossed heads apart; here voice 2's A5 quarters shift LEFT so voice 1's
// beamed C5 eighth stems clear them on the right. Mixed rhythm (8ths vs quarters)
// exercises one collision per quarter (at beats 1..4), each independently offset.
// LILYPOND-REF: lily/note-collision.cc:332-337 (meshing fallback).
octave absolute
title "Crossing-voice note collision"
part mel { clef treble }
section S {
  mel {
    voice { c'8 c' c' c' c' c' c' c' | }
    voice { a'4 a' a' a' | }
  }
}
structure { S }
score "multivoice-crossing-collision" { staff mel }
